{"id":"4fc9a0dac5607f3b","group":"92","path":"92/92-df-primitive-recursion.md","title":"Primitive Recursion","display":"df-primitive-recursion — Primitive Recursion","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Gödel's Incompleteness Theorems","book_abbrev":"92","label":"92-df-primitive-recursion","aliases":["92-df-primitive-recursion"],"display":"df-primitive-recursion — Primitive Recursion","depends_on":["[[92-df-recursion-operator]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Gödel's Incompleteness Theorems"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"92"},{"key":"label","html":"92-df-primitive-recursion"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>92-df-primitive-recursion</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-primitive-recursion — Primitive Recursion"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"8940b60e44b8fbd8\" href=\"?note=8940b60e44b8fbd8\" title=\"92-df-recursion-operator\">92-df-recursion-operator</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(k\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span> (parameter arity)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f : \\mathbb{N}^{k+1} \\to \\mathbb{N}\">\\(f : \\mathbb{N}^{k+1} \\to \\mathbb{N}\\)</span> (primitive-recursion output function)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g : \\mathbb{N}^{k} \\to \\mathbb{N}\">\\(g : \\mathbb{N}^{k} \\to \\mathbb{N}\\)</span> (base function)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"h : \\mathbb{N}^{k+2} \\to \\mathbb{N}\">\\(h : \\mathbb{N}^{k+2} \\to \\mathbb{N}\\)</span> (step function)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RecOp}_k\">\\(\\mathrm{RecOp}_k\\)</span> (recursion operator, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"8940b60e44b8fbd8\" href=\"?note=8940b60e44b8fbd8\" title=\"92-df-recursion-operator\">92-df-recursion-operator</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PrimRecEq}_k\">\\(\\mathrm{PrimRecEq}_k\\)</span> (definition-target relation)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}primitive\\text{-}recursion} \\vdash \\mathrm{PrimRecEq}_k(f,g,h)\\leftrightarrow f=\\mathrm{RecOp}_k(g,h)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}primitive\\text{-}recursion} \\vdash \\mathrm{PrimRecEq}_k(f,g,h)\\leftrightarrow f=\\mathrm{RecOp}_k(g,h)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>关键符号：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>原始递归定义模式</li>\n<li>定义新函数的基本方法</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g\">\\(g\\)</span>给出初始值</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"h\">\\(h\\)</span>给出递推规则</li>\n<li>按本书“最后一个参数递归”的约定，加法满足 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"+(x,0)=x\">\\(+(x,0)=x\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"+(x,n+1)=S(+(x,n))\">\\(+(x,n+1)=S(+(x,n))\\)</span></li>\n<li>乘法满足 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\times(x,0)=0\">\\(\\times(x,0)=0\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\times(x,n+1)=+(\\times(x,n),x)\">\\(\\times(x,n+1)=+(\\times(x,n),x)\\)</span></li>\n<li>PR 类由基本函数经有限次复合与原始递归共同生成；并非每个 PR 函数都必须由一次原始递归直接给出</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"92-df-recursion-operator","status":"resolved","id":"8940b60e44b8fbd8","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[92-df-recursion-operator]]","embed":false},{"target":"92-df-recursion-operator","status":"resolved","id":"8940b60e44b8fbd8","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\